[TEXT] I have all the evidence needed. The fault is completely clear and localized.

**Summary of findings:**
- laptop0: `default via 172.16.20.99 dev eth0` — the gateway IP 172.16.20.99 does not exist on any device in the network.
- router0 eth0.20 = 172.16.20.1/24 — the **real** VLAN 20 gateway is `.1`, not `.99`.
- laptop0 pings 172.16.20.1 successfully (L2 path is intact); 172.16.20.99 is "Destination Host Unreachable".
- VLAN 10 hosts (pc4 etc.) all use 172.16.10.1 (router0 eth0.10) — correct and working.
- mswitch1 br_vlan20 has no IP at all — consistent with router0 being the sole gateway.

